# 16. Failure Modes 🚨

Linear Regression can perform poorly when:

### ❌ Strong nonlinear relationships

Example:

```text
Complex curve
```

Possible alternatives:

- Polynomial features
- Decision Trees
- Random Forests
- Gradient Boosting
- Neural Networks

---

### ❌ Extreme Outliers

Because squared error can heavily penalize outliers.

Possible approaches:

- Investigate data quality
- Robust regression
- MAE-based objectives
- Appropriate preprocessing

---

### ❌ Data Leakage

If future information accidentally enters training, your evaluation becomes unrealistic.

---

### ❌ Distribution Shift

Training data:

```text
Old house market
```

Production data:

```text
Completely changed market
```

The learned relationship may no longer generalize.

