# 21. Explain to an Interviewer — 60-Second Script 🎤

> Linear Regression is a supervised machine-learning algorithm used to predict continuous numerical values. It learns a linear relationship between input features and a target variable, typically represented as y-hat equals XW plus b. During training, the model finds coefficients that minimize a loss function, commonly the sum or mean of squared residuals. This can be solved using methods such as ordinary least squares or iterative optimization like gradient descent. Linear Regression is simple, fast, and interpretable, making it a strong baseline model, but it may struggle with complex nonlinear relationships, significant outliers, or multicollinearity. In practice, I evaluate it using metrics such as MAE, RMSE, and R-squared and validate its performance on unseen data.

